Missing runtime error detection: 1/0 should raise ZeroDivisionError
but we removed div-by-zero property checks for Python (they're
modeled as exceptions). The exception flag is set but the assertion
still passes because the exception doesn't prevent subsequent code.
Also covers: undefined variables (NameError), negative shift,
invalid chr() args, type errors in builtins.
Affects ~92 ESBMC wrong-pass tests.
